---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import DeviceTable from "../components/DeviceTable.astro";
import { selfHostable } from "../lib/data.js";
const rows = selfHostable();
---
<Base title="Self-hostable" current="self-hostable"
      description="Devices whose vendor cloud can be replaced entirely by software you run yourself.">
  <h1>Self-hostable</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    These devices ship with a vendor cloud, so they are not D0 or D1 — but everything that
    cloud does can be replaced by software running on hardware you own. Block them at the
    firewall and you lose nothing you cannot rebuild yourself.
  </p>
  <p class="lede">
    We keep this separate from the tier on purpose. Whether you <em>can</em> firewall a
    device is a fact about the product; whether you <em>have</em> is a fact about your
    network, and the tier should mean the same thing for every reader. This page is where
    the difference lives.
  </p>
  <DeviceTable rows={rows} />
  <p class="age">
    The replacement software named on each device page is the specific thing to install —
    Frigate, Blue Iris, ZoneMinder, Home Assistant, ESPHome, ratgdo, WireGuard.
  </p>
</Base>
